Title: "Overview"
Id: "5f40c17f-8784-4957-807b-70e204f46952"

Text: "Aliases introduce alternate notation or rendering behavior.

MathLingua currently uses three alias operators:

- `:=>` for expression aliases
- `:->` for directed specification capabilities
- `:<->:` for equivalent specification capabilities
- `:~>` for writing aliases

Aliases can appear in `Aliases:`, `Requires:`, `Enables:`, `Documented:`, and
top-level `Writing:` contexts, depending on the group kind. The surrounding
structural section determines the exact meaning. `:->` infers only left to
right; `:<->:` also infers right to left when all conclusions are available."
Id: "8432dc35-def6-4279-a451-121e04d98c50"
